course: dictionary
lesson: 1775
title: One word, many meanings: click
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: The word click has more than one meaning, and the words around it tell you which one to use. Sometimes a click is a short sharp sound: «Dolphins send out fast clicks» means quick sounds that they listen to, not presses.
explain: On a computer, to click means to press the mouse button or tap the screen to choose something. «Take a ten, click on a unit with a hyphen» is a little different: it means pick a unit and join it on, like a Lego brick.
explain: Click can also mean suddenly understanding something, or two people liking each other quickly. Ask yourself: what word would fit here? Then put your meaning in the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
fact: Click can be a noun (a click) or a verb (to click).
fact: A click is a short, sharp sound, like a door shutting or fingers snapping.
fact: On a computer, to click is to press the mouse button or tap to choose something.
fact: If something clicks, you suddenly understand it.
fact: Think before you click: don't click on strange links, pop-ups or adverts, and ask an adult.
exercise: Dolphins find things by sending out fast «clicks» and listening to the echoes. What is a click here? | A slow, soft song | *A short, sharp sound | A kind of fish
exercise: «Take a ten, click on a unit with a hyphen, and you have a number.» What does click on mean here? | To shut a door loudly | *To pick and join on | To read the number aloud slowly
exercise: Max says, «It clicked when I saw the answer.» What does clicked mean? | He ran out of the room | He lost the answer | *He suddenly understood
test: Before you click on an advert on a computer, what should you do? | *Ask an adult first | Click on it quickly to see what it is | Share it with all your friends
test: In «like the click you hear when the kettle has boiled», what is the click? | *A short, sharp sound | A cup being put down | Steam coming from the spout
exam: If two people «click», what does it mean? | They always argue | *They like each other quickly | They press the same mouse button | They make a loud sound
